in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/spectral

# @mirror/spectral/portal — typed transport over a content-addressed
# subspace; portal-as-eigenvalue-stream-as-gen_prism at the mirror
# altitude; the substrate's third sub-shard of the 5-tick cascade
# closing the pretty-printer LRM.
#
# THE T18 SUB-SHARD landing the third tick of the cascade. Lifts the
# boot-altitude `@spectral/portal` declaration (with its three sibling
# wire grammars handshake/codec/stream) to the mirror altitude under
# the `@mirror/spectral` family root. Same primitive, two altitudes;
# the family root names the discipline; species parameterise the
# transport.
#
# Load-bearing recognition (per
# docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md;
# Reed 2026-06-08; commit 6d57ab4): **the open portal IS a gen_prism;
# each tick is one bidirectional update over the eigenvalue stream;
# the substrate holds superposition across the process boundary.**
# The portal type's four fields are the substrate's typed declaration
# of that recognition: a `socket` (raw transport) bound to a
# `subspace: shift(oid, fragmentation)` (the content-addressed
# identity), a `frame: shift(oid, shard)` (this end's observer
# frame), and an `actor: shift(oid, gen_prism)` (the running
# autopoietic actor). Three of four fields are `shift(oid, T)` — the
# 26th-instance substrate-pull recognition: `shift(oid, T)` is the
# substrate's typed-capability-plus-content-address primitive.
#
# === The 26th-instance recognition ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (the 26th instance):
# `shift(oid, T)` is the single primitive that does what Cap'n Proto
# needs both (capability typing + bytes) and WSTP needs (symbolic
# expression serialisation) and `SCM_RIGHTS` needs (OS-layer fd
# passing). Three of the four portal fields carry it; the substrate
# has been declaring the typed-capability primitive since
# `boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror` (2026-06-04). This shard lifts
# the recognition to the mirror altitude so consumer pulls (CLI
# pipe handoff, MCP session-typed dispatch, mosaic inter-node
# coordination) read the named primitive rather than re-deriving
# the composition from the boot floor.
#
# === The eigenvalue-projection action ===
#
# `project_eigenvalue(stream: beam<oid>) -> beam<eigenvalue>` IS the
# focus projection at the portal altitude. Per
# `boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror`'s already-declared wire
# format — *"8 bytes IEEE-754 big-endian double per value. Not
# tokens. Not bytes. Eigenvalues."* — each `shift(oid, observation)`
# the upstream gen_prism emits projects to its scalar summary (the
# eigenvalue carried over the wire). This action names that
# projection at the family altitude. Same operation
# `read_value(c) -> imperfect(f64)` realises at the wire altitude;
# this shard lifts it to a stream-of-typed-refs over a
# stream-of-eigenvalues so consumers compose it through the standard
# `beam<T>` carrier rather than the per-byte wire protocol.
#
# === Load-bearing spec ===
#
# - docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md
#   (the 26th-instance recognition; the LRM-closing arc; the
#   portal-IS-gen_prism collapse)
# - docs/insights/2026-05-26-portal-as-io-socket-over-content-
#   addressed-subspace.md (Reed + Alex + Mara, the canonical paint
#   for the four-stage wire protocol)
# - docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §3.2, §4.7 (the orchestra
#   altitude's transport surface; portals carry the substrate's
#   coordination between shards across processes)
# - ~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/fragmentation/
#   portals.md (2026-03-24; the corpus prior art; six portal
#   instances re-typed by `boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror` as
#   instantiations of this single primitive)
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Lifted from boot/std/spectral/portal/ (one tick concurrent with this
# family-altitude lift; each species declares only the names + types
# at the mirror altitude; the wire-level bodies stay in the boot
# shards for the moment per the transitional-placeholder discipline):
#
#   @mirror/spectral/portal/handshake  the WS upgrade dance (5
#                                       actions); first wire stage.
#   @mirror/spectral/portal/codec      the @fragmentation/frame <->
#                                       bytes codec (4 actions); the
#                                       middle wire stage; 96-byte
#                                       three-OID frame.
#   @mirror/spectral/portal/stream     the bidirectional eigenvalue
#                                       stream (3 actions); the wire's
#                                       runtime; 8-byte IEEE-754
#                                       per value.
#
# All three species are forward-promised at the mirror altitude;
# their boot floor remains the authoritative substrate for the wire
# protocol until consumer-pull migrations land (per
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] + the T16 transitional
# placeholder pattern).
#
# === Why one family ===
#
# Without the family, every consumer (CLI pipe handoff per T20; MCP
# session-typed dispatch per `docs/insights/2026-06-07-mcp-as-
# session-typed-prism.md`; mosaic inter-node coordination per
# `boot/std/spectral/mosaic.mirror`) re-derives the portal
# composition from the four-stage wire protocol's atomic primitives.
# With the family, the discipline IS the family: the portal carrier
# names the typed-capability primitive (`shift(oid, T)` in three
# fields); the project_eigenvalue action names the focus projection
# at the transport altitude; the wire species discharge the
# byte-level realisation. Consumers compose at the family altitude
# rather than the boot altitude.
#
# === The pretty-printer cascade ===
#
# This shard is T18 in the 5-tick cascade closing the pretty-printer
# LRM (per docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-
# prism.md):
#
#   T16 ✓ — @mirror/data root + json lift + yaml/toml/text stubs
#   T17 ✓ — @code/mirror.render with Wadler/Bernardy combinators
#   T18 ← — portal eigenvalue projection at substrate altitude (this)
#   T19 — `mirror kintsugi <file>` settled-formatting output path
#   T20 — portal handoff via SCM_RIGHTS at CLI pipe boundary
#
# T19 reads `project_eigenvalue` as the substrate-typed contract the
# terminal-collapse path realises (the `mirror kintsugi <file>` write
# emits through the Wadler/Bernardy render at T17; the portal pipe
# path emits through this projection). T20 lands the OS-layer
# realisation (`SCM_RIGHTS` for the socket field; the substrate's
# `shift(oid, T)` triple flows over the wire without re-serialisation).
#
# === Sibling relationship to sibling sub-shards ===
#
# `@mirror/spectral/oscillate` runs the kintsugi loop; `@mirror/
# spectral/consent` is the Φ query; `@mirror/spectral/score` is the
# orchestra's shared state; `@mirror/spectral/morphism` is the
# per-candidate carrier. This shard is the TRANSPORT surface — what
# carries oscillation's per-tick eigenvalue stream, consent's
# pending morphism_set, score's anchor refs, and morphism's
# pre/post-anchor pairs across process boundaries when the
# orchestra spans more than one local shard.
#
# The dependency points inward: this shard does NOT pull
# `oscillate` / `consent` / `score` / `morphism`; THEY may pull
# `portal` when their composition crosses a process boundary. The
# transport surface is the substrate's most foundational sibling
# under @mirror/spectral; it pulls only @mirror/spectral (the family
# root) and surfaces the @spectral/portal/{handshake,codec,stream}
# boot grammars by sub-shard mirror altitude lifts.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (26th instance):
# the substrate had `shift(oid, T)` declared in three portal fields
# since 2026-06-04; this shard names the recognition at the mirror
# altitude. Per [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: the boot floor's
# composition is authoritative; this shard lifts the named primitives
# to the family altitude without inventing types. Per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: the project_eigenvalue body is
# `\` — lands when the T19/T20 consumer pulls. Per
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]: the same lift that gave
# @cli → @mirror/lens/cli, @loss → @mirror/loss, @data → @mirror/data;
# grammar-altitude @spectral/portal → mirror-altitude @mirror/
# spectral/portal.
#
# === Transitional retention of boot/std/spectral/portal* ===
#
# All four boot shards (portal.mirror + portal/{handshake, codec,
# stream}.mirror) are RETAINED, not retired. Reasons:
#
#   - No external consumer of `@spectral/portal` yet: the boot file
#     imports its own sub-grammars (`in @spectral/portal/handshake`
#     etc); no other shard imports them. The lift is purely
#     additive — no boot consumer breaks.
#   - The wire-protocol bodies (handshake's UTF-8 substrate gap;
#     codec's oid<->bytes substrate gap; stream's bounded-iteration
#     substrate gap) live at the boot altitude per the substrate-
#     pull discipline. The mirror-altitude family names the typed
#     surface; the boot altitude carries the byte-level
#     realisation. Consumer-pull migrations from `in @spectral/
#     portal` to `in @mirror/spectral/portal` land tick-by-tick as
#     the wire-protocol substrate gaps close.
#   - The same pattern held for @cli (kept in boot during lens
#     migration), @loss (kept in boot during loss family lift), and
#     @data/json (kept in boot during data family lift). Boot files
#     retire one consumer-pull at a time, not at the family-root
#     lift.
#
# When the wire-protocol substrate gaps close (UTF-8 codec lands for
# handshake; oid <-> bytes lands for codec; bounded-iteration lands
# for stream — all per Scheduler Tower spec), the boot floor's
# bodies fill and the mirror-altitude species can take over the
# authoritative carrier role.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Each face of the portal recognition has prior art; no system
# composes them all the way the substrate does:
#
#   portal-as-actor     Hewitt 1973 actor model; Hewitt-Bishop-
#                       Steiger "A Universal Modular Actor
#                       Formalism for Artificial Intelligence"
#                       (IJCAI). Erlang's gen_server (Armstrong
#                       1986+); BEAM's typed-mailbox actor;
#                       gen_prism specialises the autopoietic
#                       case per Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984.
#   eigenvalue stream   GRAM-style multi-trajectory inference;
#                       Wolfram WSTP (Wolfram Symbolic Transfer
#                       Protocol; ~1991) for typed inter-process
#                       symbolic pipes; closest existing
#                       substrate-typed IPC.
#   shift(oid, T)       Cap'n Proto RPC (Varda 2013+) for typed
#                       capabilities over bytes; IPFS (Benet 2014)
#                       for content addressing; substrate collapses
#                       the two seams into a single operator.
#   session types       Honda 1993; Wadler 2012 "Propositions as
#                       Sessions" (ICFP); the formal grounding for
#                       holding superposition through the pipe.
#   wire format         WebSocket (RFC 6455, 2011) for the socket
#                       handshake; Erlang Distribution Protocol
#                       (BEAM, 1990s) for the typed-message wire;
#                       9P/Plan 9 (Pike 1985) for namespaced
#                       file-as-service.
#
# Spec context: docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-
#               gen-prism.md (the 26th-instance recognition),
#               docs/insights/2026-05-26-portal-as-io-socket-over-
#               content-addressed-subspace.md (the canonical paint),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-07-mcp-as-session-typed-prism.md
#               (the session-typed sibling at the MCP altitude),
#               docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md (the orchestra
#               altitude this transport serves).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (the same lift; transport-altitude instance).
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (26th instance: `shift(oid, T)` as typed-
#                      capability primitive),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (lift from boot
#                      floor; no invention),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
#                      (project_eigenvalue body is `\`; lands when
#                      T19/T20 consumer pulls).
# Forward-promise to consumers:
#   - T19 `mirror kintsugi <file>` reads `project_eigenvalue` as
#     the typed contract for the terminal-collapse path's eigenvalue
#     emission (vs the Wadler/Bernardy render emission).
#   - T20 `SCM_RIGHTS` pipe handoff lands the OS-layer realisation;
#     the substrate's `shift(oid, T)` triple flows over the wire
#     without re-serialisation; the receiving end reads
#     `project_eigenvalue` as the typed contract for the inbound
#     stream.
#   - Mosaic inter-node coordination (per
#     `boot/std/spectral/mosaic.mirror`) reads this transport when
#     the orchestra spans more than one local shard.
#   - MCP session-typed dispatch (per docs/insights/2026-06-07-mcp-
#     as-session-typed-prism.md) reads this transport when the
#     session crosses a process boundary.
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the family root; this
#                 shard is a species under it),
#                 mirror/spectral/oscillate.mirror (the loop primitive
#                 whose per-tick eigenvalue stream this transport
#                 carries when the loop spans processes),
#                 mirror/spectral/score.mirror (the orchestra's
#                 shared score; refs across this transport carry
#                 score updates between processes),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (the Φ query; the
#                 morphism_set this transport carries per consent
#                 surface evaluation),
#                 mirror/spectral/morphism.mirror (the per-candidate
#                 carrier; pre/post-anchor pairs flow over this
#                 transport for cross-process identity_preserving),
#                 mirror/data.mirror (the sibling content-format
#                 family; the terminal collapse picks a @mirror/data
#                 species when crossing a non-mirror boundary),
#                 boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror (the floor
#                 declaration this species lifts; retained as
#                 transitional placeholder during consumer-pull
#                 migration),
#                 boot/std/spectral/portal/{handshake, codec,
#                 stream}.mirror (the wire-protocol sub-grammars
#                 the boot floor authoritatively declares; the
#                 mirror-altitude species under this shard surface
#                 their typed contracts but defer the byte-level
#                 bodies until the wire-protocol substrate gaps
#                 close).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/portal.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/spectral/portal` as a species under the `@mirror/spectral`
# family; sub-species live at
# `shards/mirror/spectral/portal/<name>.mirror`.

prism @mirror/spectral/portal {
  focus portal
  project portal
  split portal
  shift portal
  settle portal
}

# === The portal carrier ===
#
# Four fields. The substrate's typed declaration of the
# portal-as-eigenvalue-stream-as-gen_prism recognition:
#
# socket   — the raw transport underneath (the @io/socket.connection
#             duplex byte stream). Re-types `@io.socket` to the
#             connection-oriented handle from the substrate's #81
#             tick. NOT carried as `shift(oid, T)` because the
#             socket is the substrate that carries the shifts, not
#             a shift itself; the boundary is the transport layer.
# subspace — `shift(oid, fragmentation)` — the content-addressed
#             identity of the fragmentation subspace this portal
#             points at. The 26th-instance primitive's first field:
#             the classical bit per portals.md's "teleportation"
#             framing; the receiver dereferences the OID through
#             `@fragmentation.observe` and the state was never
#             moved — only the address.
# frame    — `shift(oid, shard)` — this end's observer frame. The
#             OID of `@mirror/shard.self()` at portal-open time.
#             Comparing observations across portals walks the
#             shard parent chain per `@time.convert` (the substrate's
#             relativistic-frame-conversion primitive).
# actor    — `shift(oid, gen_prism)` — the connection's autopoietic
#             actor. **The open portal IS this gen_prism**; each
#             tick is one bidirectional update over the eigenvalue
#             stream. Autopoietic close fires when Reflection picks
#             `settle(self)` OR the host shard's
#             `compute_bound.max_reductions` exhausts.
#
# Identity contract: two portals are equal iff all four fields
# match. Three of the four are `shift(oid, T)`; the OID-quadruple
# determines the portal's identity at the substrate altitude.
# `content_addressed(portal)` (per `boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror`'s
# `requires` block) is structurally satisfied.
type portal = {
  socket:   ref,
  subspace: shift(oid, fragmentation),
  frame:    shift(oid, shard),
  actor:    shift(oid, gen_prism),
}

# === project_eigenvalue — the focus projection at the portal altitude ===
#
# Reads a beam of typed-capability refs (each carrying a
# `shift(oid, observation)`) and emits a beam of eigenvalue scalars
# — the wire-altitude representation of the upstream gen_prism's
# per-tick observations.
#
# Note on type parameters: both stream-in and stream-out are typed
# `beam` (bare). The substrate's `type beam(t)` declaration in
# `boot/std/beam.mirror` is parametric, but the action-signature
# grammar at this altitude does not yet accept `beam<T>` / `beam(t)`
# at use-sites (parser gap; consumer-pull when the parametric-
# use-site rule lands). The bare `beam` is the substrate's existing
# convention everywhere `beam` is used in an action signature today
# (cf. @beam.observe, @beam.compare). The semantic content of the
# projection — refs in, eigenvalues out — is named in this doc and
# discharged when the consumer pulls.
#
# IS the focus operation in the five-op block at the portal
# altitude. Per `boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror`'s already-
# declared wire format (*"8 bytes IEEE-754 big-endian double per
# value. Not tokens. Not bytes. Eigenvalues."*), each
# `shift(oid, observation)` the upstream gen_prism emits projects
# to its scalar summary; the projection IS the focus at the wire
# altitude.
#
# Connection to the 26th-instance recognition: per the insight doc
# (`docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md`
# §"The 26th instance — `shift(oid, T)`"), three of the four portal
# fields carry typed-capability refs. The fourth — the eigenvalue
# stream — is what this action projects from. Each f64 eigenvalue
# IS a `shift(oid, observation)` projected to its scalar summary;
# the substrate's typed-capability primitive flows through the
# wire as the eigenvalue stream's per-tick payload.
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. For each `shift(oid, observation)` in the input beam: read
#      the observation's eigenvalue summary (the @epistemologic/
#      math/spectrum scalar the substrate already crystallises per
#      tick); emit as f64 on the output beam.
#   2. The bounded-iteration discipline IS structural — per
#      `@epistemologic/property/halts`'s disjunction (autopoietic
#      settlement OR budget exhaustion), the projection terminates
#      by construction.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# each input ref through the @fragmentation.observe surface, the
# observation's eigenvalue summary through the @epistemologic/math/
# spectrum projection, and emits the f64 on the output beam. The
# substrate names the surface; the bytes are the wire's concern
# (per `boot/std/spectral/portal/stream.mirror`'s
# `read_value` / `write_value` realisation).
#
# Consumers (forward-promised):
#
#   - T19 `mirror kintsugi <file>` reads this as the typed contract
#     for the terminal-collapse path's eigenvalue emission (the
#     alternative to the Wadler/Bernardy render emission at T17).
#   - T20 `SCM_RIGHTS` pipe handoff: the inbound side reads this
#     as the typed contract for the eigenvalue stream arriving
#     over the wire; the substrate state never serialises to bytes
#     between mirror processes.
#   - MCP session-typed dispatch (per docs/insights/2026-06-07-mcp-
#     as-session-typed-prism.md): the per-session eigenvalue stream
#     surfaces through this projection when the session crosses a
#     process boundary.
project_eigenvalue(stream: beam) -> beam { \ }

out @mirror/spectral/portal
out portal
out project_eigenvalue
